  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#22201\", \"PowerToys#25363\", \"PowerToys#34814\"], \"answer\": \"Yes, this has been requested many times, and the PowerToys team has declined it. Renaming a zip to exe or msi doesn't convert anything. Real conversions such as DOC to PDF need format-specific logic, codecs and sometimes licenses. They can also lose data, and the team doesn't plan to build a universal file converter. Most of those requests were closed as duplicates of #9743. Use the app that opened the file and its Save As or Export option (for example, Word can save as PDF). Otherwise use a dedicated converter tool. If you only want to change extensions, PowerRename can do it, including for many files at once. Set 'Apply to' to 'Filename + extension', turn on regex, and search for something like \\\\.txt$ to replace it. In File Explorer you can also rename a single file by hand. Be aware that renaming a file doesn't change its actual format.\"}",
